ull,{"post":{"slug":"stay-consistent-with-workouts","category":"CONSISTENCY","title":"How to stay consistent with workouts when life gets busy","description":"Practical ways to stay consistent with workouts using shorter sessions, flexible weekly targets and realistic fitness habits.","lead":"A flexible routine survives busy weeks better than a perfect routine that only works on perfect days.","keywords":["workout consistency","fitness motivation","stay consistent with exercise","fitness habits"],"stage":6,"activity":"stretch","takeaway":"Consistency is a system, not a personality trait.","sections":[{"heading":"Lower the minimum on hard days","body":"Your shortest useful session should be easy enough to start when motivation is low. Ten minutes of movement can protect the habit without pretending every day is a full training day."},{"heading":"Track weeks, not perfect streaks","body":"A weekly target gives you room to move sessions when work, school, travel or family plans change."},{"heading":"Make the next action obvious","body":"Prepare the workout, clothing or space before you need it. Reducing setup makes it easier to begin when energy is limited."},{"heading":"Let identity follow behavior","body":"You do not need to feel like a fitness person before training. Repeated small actions are what gradually make the routine feel normal."}]},"index":5,"total":14,"prevHref":"/blog/beginner-bodyweight-workout-plan","nextHref":"/blog/10-minute-workout-busy-days"}],["$L5"],"$L6"]}],{},null,false,null]},null,false,"$7"]},null,false,"$7"]},null,false,null],"$L8",false]],"m":"$undefined","G":["$9",["$La"]],"S":true,"h":null,"r":"$undefined","s":"$undefined","a":"$undefined","l":"$undefined","p":"$undefined","d":"$undefined","b":"Nd1cQcP5Lh31_JTWc3jWW"}
